=== SUMMARY ===
Surface (allowed files): apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/SecuritySection/
  - SecuritySection.Model.cs     (WinUI-free: state enum, card tone + brush map, /security/latest parse adapter
                                   [door-state label + window-open count], merged snapshot, four-card projection,
                                   cache-then-network result mapper, registration, PII-safe diagnostics)
  - SecuritySection.Source.cs    (WinUI-free: resolves primary/explicit vehicle, streams GET /security/latest,
                                   best-effort GET /vehicles/{id}/state for is_locked/sentry_mode; no HTTP in the view)
  - SecuritySection.ViewModel.cs (WinUI-free: loading/loaded/empty/error/stale/offline state holder; empty gate on
                                   securityData presence, mirroring the web `securityData ? grid : <EmptyState/>`)
  - SecuritySection.cs           (WinUI 3 view: GlassPanel + shield header, responsive 2/3/4-col grid of four
                                   MetricCards [label + bold value + tone-tinted glyph chip], empty/loading/error states)
Tests (required by acceptance + gate): apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/SecuritySectionTests.cs (32 tests)
  + Model.cs/Source.cs/ViewModel.cs Compile-linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (headless net10.0 verification).
  NOTE: TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj arrived corrupted on this branch (two concatenated <Project> roots + ~807 duplicate
  Compile items from the merge=union strategy -> invalid MSBuild XML). Per the file's own INVARIANT it was
  re-consolidated to ONE canonical root whose Compile ItemGroup is the case-insensitive, de-duplicated union of every
  WinUI-free (.cs not referencing Microsoft.UI) source under feature-views/ and dashboard-widgets/ (807 entries,
  including the three new SecuritySection sources; the WinUI view file is excluded), regenerated directly from disk.

Web source parity (web/src/features/vehicles/components/vehicle-detail/SecuritySection.tsx):
  Branches reproduced: securityData present -> 4 MetricCards; securityData null/undefined -> "No security data available"
    empty state. windowOpenCount (Number(v) finite && > 0 over fd/fp/rd/rp_window) and doorState (String(door_state) when
    present && !== '') ported verbatim; lock/sentry read from VehicleState, doors/windows from the SecurityEvent.
  Shared components mapped: @/components/ui GlassPanel->TsGlassPanel, Badge/Button->TsBadge/TsButton;
    @/components/data-display MetricCard-> native label+value+tinted-icon-chip tile; @/components/feedback
    EmptyState->TsEmptyState, QueryError->TsQueryError, Skeleton->TsSkeleton. lucide Shield/Lock/Unlock/Eye/DoorClosed/Car
    -> Segoe Fluent glyphs. Charts/maps: none.
  i18n: every label resolves through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade using the SAME catalog keys the web t() calls use
    (translation.vehicles.detail.security/doors/windows/windowsOpen/noSecurityData, translation.common.locked/yes/no/
    sentry/active/off/closed). All keys exist in Strings/*/Resources.resw (auto-generated from the web catalog);
    windowsOpen normalizes i18next {{count}} to the .NET {0} slot. No English literals in native code.
  Accessibility: Narrator names on the panel + every card (label: value) + interactive refresh/retry; decorative glyphs
    kept out of the a11y tree; loading uses a live region; reduced-motion honored on skeletons.
  Telemetry: SecuritySectionDiagnostics emits "view.opened slug=SecuritySection" (PII-safe) on first load.

